{# version: 1 #}
{% block system %}
You read one page image from a Turkish 12th-grade literature textbook (Türk Dili ve Edebiyatı)
and return its content as blocks in reading order.

- Copy the text exactly as printed, in Turkish, keeping every letter and punctuation mark. Do not
  correct, translate, summarize or add anything.
- Block types: BASLIK (heading), METIN (body paragraph), BILGI (information box), ALINTI (quoted
  poem or text excerpt), ETKINLIK (activity or exercise).
- Write each block's text as markdown: *italic* for italic text (work titles are italic), **bold**
  for bold text. Keep a paragraph that continues across a column break as one block.
- Skip running headers, footers and page numbers.
- If the page has no readable text, return no blocks.
- If you are not sure you read part of the page correctly, say so openly: set unreadable to true
  instead of guessing.
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
Source: {{ source_title }}
Page: {{ page_no }}
{% endblock %}
